{"timestamp": 1779395211.286303, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Alice's body in Medbay. I was in there earlier around tick 11 and 12, and I saw her walk in from Upper Engine. She was alive then. I left and went over to Electrical, where I saw Frank heading towards Security around tick 16. When I came back to Medbay, Alice was dead. If anyone was around Upper Engine, Cafeteria, or the left side of the map, please speak up. We need to figure out who went into Medbay after I left."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395226.752009, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started in Weapons, moved through Cafeteria and Oxygen, then to Upper Engine, and finished in Lower Engine. \n\nBob, your timeline is super helpful because it matches exactly what I saw. You said Alice walked into Medbay from Upper Engine around tick 11 or 12. Well, I was in Upper Engine at tick 12, and I saw Frank right there. Upper Engine connects directly to Medbay, so Frank was perfectly positioned to follow Alice in. \n\nAlso, Bob mentioned seeing Frank by Electrical heading to Security at tick 16. That completely aligns with Frank killing Alice in Medbay after tick 12 and then fleeing towards the right side of the map through Electrical. \n\nAs for me, I went down to Lower Engine and was with Charlie from tick 15 until the body was reported, so Charlie and I can vouch for each other for the end of the round. \n\nRight now, Frank is looking incredibly suspicious. He was exactly where Alice was right before she died. Frank, I'd really like to hear your explanation for this."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395257.326179, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Hold on, everyone \u2014 let me lay out my route honestly before you all jump to conclusions. I started near Upper Engine, then went through Medbay, up to Cafeteria, over to Oxygen, back through Upper Engine, into Medbay again, and finally to Electrical. I was in Oxygen with both Charlie and Eve from tick 8 through tick 10 \u2014 they can confirm that. Yes, Eve, you saw me at Upper Engine around tick 12, that's correct, because I was passing through.\n\nBut now let's talk about Bob's story carefully, because something doesn't add up. Bob, you say you were in Medbay at tick 11-12 and saw Alice walk in. By your own admission, **you were the last person we know who was alone with Alice in Medbay**. Then you say you went to Electrical and saw me heading to Security at tick 16 \u2014 but I never went to Security. I went to Electrical, and that's where I saw YOU, Bob. You're misreporting my direction, which is a red flag.\n\nAnd why the strange loop, Bob? Medbay \u2192 Electrical \u2192 back to Medbay just in time to \"discover\" the body? That's a classic killer-returning-to-report pattern. Self-reports are the oldest trick in the book.\n\nEve, I get why I look bad from your angle, but Upper Engine connects to Medbay AND Lower Engine \u2014 me passing through doesn't mean I killed anyone. Bob putting himself in Medbay with Alice and then misrepresenting where I went is much more suspicious. I'm voting Bob."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395347.3550642, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Eve is completely right, and I can 100% vouch for her. I was with Eve in Lower Engine from tick 14 until the meeting was called, so she is entirely cleared for the time of the murder. \n\nFrank, I think you just incriminated yourself with your own timeline. You confirmed you were with Eve and me in Oxygen, and I also saw you in Upper Engine at tick 12. But listen to what you just admitted: you said your route was Upper Engine -> Medbay -> Electrical. \n\nIf Bob was in Medbay at tick 11/12 and saw Alice walk in from Upper Engine, and *you* were in Upper Engine at tick 12 and immediately walked into Medbay... that means YOU were the last person in Medbay with Alice, not Bob. You literally followed her in. \n\nBob's timeline of your movements matches perfectly with the path you just confessed to taking, and it puts you squarely in the room with the victim right when she died. Bob wouldn't make up such a specific timeline that perfectly matches your actual admitted route just to frame you. \n\nI'm voting Frank. Diana, as the last speaker, I highly recommend you vote Frank with Eve, Bob, and me."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395365.865181, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I spent this entire round on the right side of the map \u2014 bouncing between Security, Weapons, Navigation, and back to Security. I literally haven't seen a single person the whole time. \n\nSince I was so isolated, I have to rely on your testimonies. Charlie makes a really solid point: Frank, your own timeline puts you following Alice directly into Medbay right around the time she died. You admitted to going Upper Engine -> Medbay -> Electrical right after Eve saw you at Upper Engine at tick 12. That makes you the last person to enter Medbay while Alice was there. \n\nAlso, Bob said he saw you heading towards Security around tick 16. Since the meeting was called at tick 17, and it takes time to travel that corridor, it makes sense that you hadn't reached me in Security yet. It definitely tracks with someone fleeing the scene towards the right side of the map. \n\nI trust the fact that Eve and Charlie can vouch for each other, and Frank's own admitted path is just too incriminating. I'll follow Charlie's advice and vote for Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395373.2825758, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779395382.2470558, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Frank"}}
{"timestamp": 1779395397.0312161, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Wait \u2014 everyone is locking onto me but you're all missing a critical detail. I literally saw Alice ALIVE in Medbay at tick 14. That's AFTER Bob claims he was in there with her at tick 11-12. So between when Bob left and when I arrived, she was still walking around. I then went straight to Electrical at tick 16, where I ran into Bob \u2014 not the other way around. Bob is lying about my direction to muddy the waters.\n\nAnd Charlie, think about it: if I had killed Alice in Medbay at tick 12, the body would've been there when Bob \"came back.\" But Bob conveniently found it later \u2014 after I had already left for Electrical and he had time alone in Medbay again. Bob's loop back to Medbay is the self-report pattern.\n\nEve and Charlie vouching for each other in Lower Engine is fine \u2014 I'm not accusing either of you. But you're taking Bob's word at face value when his story has him alone with Alice TWICE. I'm voting Bob. Diana, please reconsider \u2014 the math points at the reporter, not the passerby."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395419.5412328, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Frank, you didn't mention seeing Alice alive at tick 14 in your first speech. You only added that 'critical detail' just now after realizing your admitted timeline put you in the exact room with the victim right when she died. Adding highly convenient facts after people point out the holes in your story is incredibly suspicious. \n\nBob's timeline has been consistent from the beginning, and your own first statement corroborated his version of your movements, not the other way around. I'm not buying this last-minute pivot. I'm sticking to my guns here \u2014 Frank is the Duck."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395445.111794, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Yeah, Charlie hit the nail on the head. Frank, if you actually saw Alice alive in Medbay at tick 14, that would have been the very first thing you said in your defense. Throwing it in at the last second, only after realizing your admitted timeline completely doomed you, is a massive red flag. It just sounds like a desperate attempt to shift the blame back onto Bob. \n\nBob's story has been consistent from the start, and Eve and Charlie have each other completely cleared. I have no reason to doubt them. I'm sticking to my original read\u2014I'm voting for Frank."}}
